          "line": 66,
          "page": null,
          "excerpt": "When the context hits 85%, the middleware picks a cutoff point that keeps the most recent messages intact and summarizes older messages into a single block. The messages being summarized are appended to /conversation\\_history/{session\\_id}.md on the filesystem. The middleware generates the session ID internally. The summary message the model receives includes a link to that file, so the agent can read those older sections back with read\\_file if it needs the detail. Because a summary is far more compact than the messages it replaces, the token count drops sharply and the conversation can continue.",
          "material_id": "lessons/m3.1-summarization-context-offloading",
          "category": "lessons",
          "source_url": "https://github.com/langchain-ai/lca-deepagents/blob/HEAD/thinkific/src/m3/m3.1-summarization-context-offloading.md",
          "sha256": "ae56f3c58a89d7b6baf2c25b0c5261e7a2912f2d249cc15759fcda542d89d4e9"
        }
